### ============================================================
###  COMMON API — Online Learning Platform
###  Base URL : http://localhost:1935/auth
###  Auth     : Bearer token in Authorization header
###             Token is returned by /login; store it and send as:
###             Authorization: Bearer <token>
###  Roles    : STUDENT | INSTRUCTOR | ADMIN
### ============================================================

### ── REGISTER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [1] Register a new STUDENT
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Arjun",
    "lastName": "Mehta",
    "email": "arjun.mehta@example.com",
    "password": "Student@123",
    "role": "STUDENT",
    "profileImageUrl": "https://example.com/avatars/arjun.png",
    "headline": "Aspiring Full-Stack Developer",
    "bio": "I love learning new technologies and building web apps.",
    "location": "Hyderabad, Telangana",
    "phone": "9876543210"
}

###

### [2] Register a new INSTRUCTOR
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Priya",
    "lastName": "Sharma",
    "email": "priya.sharma@example.com",
    "password": "Instructor@456",
    "role": "INSTRUCTOR",
    "profileImageUrl": "https://example.com/avatars/priya.png",
    "headline": "Senior Software Engineer & Educator",
    "bio": "10+ years of experience in Java, Spring Boot, and Microservices.",
    "location": "Bangalore, Karnataka",
    "phone": "9988776655"
}

###

### [3] Register an ADMIN
###     NOTE: The register route blocks ADMIN by default (allowedRoles check).
###           Seed the first admin directly via the database or a trusted script.
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Admin",
    "lastName": "User",
    "email": "admin@olp.com",
    "password": "Admin@789",
    "role": "ADMIN",
    "profileImageUrl": "https://example.com/avatars/admin.png"
}

###

### ── LOGIN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  The response body contains { token: "..." }.
###  Copy that token and paste it into the Authorization header below.

### [4] Login — Student
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "arjun.mehta@example.com",
    "password": "Student@123"
}

###

### [5] Login — Instructor
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "priya.sharma@example.com",
    "password": "Instructor@456"
}

###

### [6] Login — Admin
POST http://localhost:1935/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "admin@olp.com",
    "password": "Admin@789"
}

###

### ── LOGOUT / SESSION ─────────────────────────────────────────

### [7] Logout
###     Server returns success; frontend removes the token from localStorage.
GET http://localhost:1935/auth/logout

###

### [8] Check Auth — verify the Bearer token is still valid
###     Returns { message: "authenticated", payload: <decoded JWT> }
###     Replace <token> with the value from your last /login response.
GET http://localhost:1935/auth/check-auth
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### ── PASSWORD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [9] Change Password (must be logged in)
###     Verifies currentPassword before applying the update.
PUT http://localhost:1935/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "currentPassword": "Student@123",
    "newPassword": "UpdatedStudent@321"
}

###

### [10] Forgot Password (no login required)
###      Only works when ENABLE_FORGOT_PASSWORD=true in .env.
###      In production, keep this disabled and use a proper OTP flow.
PUT http://localhost:1935/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "arjun.mehta@example.com",
    "newPassword": "ResetStudent@999"
}

###

### ── PUBLIC COURSES ───────────────────────────────────────────

### [11] Get All Active Courses (no auth required)
###      Used on the homepage course preview / hero section.
GET http://localhost:1935/auth/courses

###

### ── PROFILE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [12] Get Logged-in User Profile (any role)
GET http://localhost:1935/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [13] Update Logged-in User Profile (any role)
###      Allowed fields: firstName, lastName, email, profileImageUrl,
###                      headline, bio, location, phone.
###      Returns a fresh token with updated data.
PUT http://localhost:1935/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "firstName": "Arjun",
    "lastName": "Mehta",
    "email": "arjun.mehta@example.com",
    "profileImageUrl": "https://example.com/avatars/arjun-v2.png",
    "headline": "Full-Stack Developer | React & Node.js",
    "bio": "Passionate about building scalable web applications.",
    "location": "Chennai, Tamil Nadu",
    "phone": "9123456789"
}
